<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hulü Guang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">515–572</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hulü <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-people">Guang</a> was one of the leading generals of the Northern Qi dynasty in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, repeatedly defeating the rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a>. The son of the general Hulü Jin, he became chancellor, and his daughter married the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-wei">Gao Wei</a>. Distrusted at court and slandered with the help of Northern Zhou propaganda, he was executed in 572; Northern Zhou conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a> five years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hulu-guang.jpg" alt="Hulü Guang" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%96%9B%E5%BE%8B%E5%85%89%EF%BC%88%E5%8C%97%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
